CoCothello Release Notes

V1.1

This release contains two major changes. The first is support for the
CMP palette set. A new screen asks for the type of monitor you are using,
either RGB or CMP. The second is in the way the computer makes its
move. It first "flashes" its move with one of its pieces. It then
waits for a mouse click before it show the results of its move.


V1.2

This release adds some options, plus fixes a minor buglet. There was
a bug in the logic which decides which message to display when the game
is won. Only two of a possible fives messages were ever being displayed.

I had some negative comments about the change in the previous version
which causes the program to wait for a mouse click before showing the
results of the computer move. I have made this a run-time option which
can be specified on the parameters line of the AIF. An F means to play
in "FAST" mode, which was the way V1.0 did it. To maintain the wait
for mouse click, use a S for "SLOW" mode. If no option for play mode
is specified, the default it "FAST".

There is another option which can be specified on the parameters line,
too. It specifies the default monitor type. An R specifies RGB, and a
C specifies CMP. If no option for monitor type is present, you will
be asked what kind of monitor you are using, just like V1.1 did.

All options may be specified in upper or lower case, and if multiple options
are present, ie, one for play mode and the other for default monitor type,
then do not put any spaces between them.


Enjoy!!!
